From: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: remoteproc: wcss-sec: allow one optional clock

Use the shared generic binding instead of adding a second schema matching
the same compatibles. IPQ5332 supplies only the sleep clock; the driver's
interconnect clock is optional. Allow a single clock/name as the previous
IPQ5332 binding did, and as the shared binding's IPQ5424 example does.

Signed-off-by: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
---
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,wcss-sec-pil.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,wcss-sec-pil.yaml
@@ -46,11 +46,13 @@ properties:
       - const: stop-ack
 
   clocks:
+    minItems: 1
     items:
       - description: sleep clock
       - description: AHB interconnect between system NOC and WCSS block
 
   clock-names:
+    minItems: 1
     items:
       - const: sleep
       - const: interconnect
